**Document ID:** SALES-003  
**Title:** Churn Analysis and Retention Performance - Fiscal Year 2024  
**Author:** Manus AI, on behalf of MedSync Health Sales & Customer Success  
**Date:** January 17, 2026  
**Status:** Final

---

## 1. Executive Summary

This report provides a comprehensive analysis of MedSync Health's customer retention and churn performance for Fiscal Year 2024. The analysis confirms the company's strong value proposition, as evidenced by a **Net Revenue Retention (NRR) of 118%**, indicating successful expansion within the existing customer base. However, the data also highlights a persistent challenge in customer volume retention, with a **Logo Retention Rate of 87%** and **Customer Retention Rate of 91%**. The primary driver of logo churn is identified within the high-volume Clinics segment, particularly among users of MedSync Analytics, which correlates with the product's lower Net Promoter Score (NPS) of 68. Strategic mitigation efforts, led by the Customer Success and Sales teams, are critical to stabilize the customer base and maximize the value of the high NRR performance.

---

## 2. Key Retention Metrics (FY 2024)

The following metrics, consistent with the Master Data Consistency Framework, define our retention performance for the fiscal year [1]. The intentional differences between the Logo and Customer Retention Rates reflect the higher churn volume in the lower-ACV Clinics segment, while the strong NRR demonstrates significant upselling and cross-selling success within the higher-ACV Hospital and Insurance Provider segments.

| Metric | Value | Interpretation |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Logo Retention Rate** | **87%** | Percentage of unique customer organizations (logos) retained. |
| **Customer Retention Rate** | **91%** | Percentage of total customer count retained (weighted by volume). |
| **Gross Revenue Retention (GRR)** | **94%** | Revenue retained from the previous year, excluding any expansion revenue. |
| **Net Revenue Retention (NRR)** | **118%** | Total revenue retained, including expansion revenue (upsells/cross-sells), net of churn and contraction. |

The NRR of 118% signifies that the revenue generated from the retained customer base grew by 18% year-over-year, successfully offsetting the revenue loss from churned customers (GRR of 94%). This performance is a testament to the value of our multi-product strategy and the success of the Sales team's land-and-expand motions.

