## 3. Customer Churn Analysis

### 3.1. Churn Volume and Impact

In FY 2024, MedSync Health experienced a total of **385 churned customer organizations** against a starting base of 3,425, resulting in a net addition of 505 customers (890 new customers acquired).

| Customer Segment | Churned Customers (Count) | Total Segment Customers (EOP) | Churn Rate (Approx.) |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Clinics** | 300 | 3,200 | 9.4% |
| **Hospitals** | 45 | 520 | 8.7% |
| **Insurance Providers** | 40 | 210 | 19.0% |
| **Total** | **385** | **3,930** | **9.8%** (Logo Churn Rate: 13%) |

The **Clinics** segment accounts for the vast majority of churn volume (78%), consistent with their lower Average Contract Value (ACV) of AED 73,500 and higher sensitivity to pricing and integration complexity. Conversely, the **Insurance Providers** segment, while having a lower volume, exhibits the highest proportional churn rate, suggesting a need for targeted retention strategies for these high-value accounts (ACV: AED 551,250).

### 3.2. Churn by Product Line

Analysis of churned accounts reveals a concentration of churn within specific product lines, suggesting product-market fit or usability challenges in certain areas.

| Product Line | Churned Customers (Count) | NPS (Q4 2024) | Primary Churn Driver |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **MedSync Analytics** | 120 | 68 | Data complexity, integration issues |
| **MedSync Connect** | 100 | 72 | Competitor displacement, lack of feature parity |
| **MedSync Patient Portal** | 80 | 75 | Low patient adoption, perceived low ROI |
| **MedSync Compliance Suite** | 85 | 70 | Regulatory changes, internal process shifts |
| **Total** | **385** | **71 (Overall)** | |

The highest volume of churn is associated with **MedSync Analytics** (120 customers), which also holds the lowest NPS of 68. This strong correlation suggests that product-related friction is a significant driver of customer attrition. (See PROD-ANALYTICS for detailed product roadmap and planned feature enhancements).

